-- cinetrack:version 28
-- cinetrack:name add accent and case insensitive library title sort key
-- The library page's "title" sort compared titles byte by byte (BINARY), so
-- "Éternels" and "amélie" sorted after every title starting with a capital
-- letter, "Zorro" included. `title_sort` is the title lower-cased and with
-- its Latin accents and ligatures folded (é to e, ß to ss, ...): a virtual
-- generated column, so nothing writes it and every existing row has it, and
-- the sort index below is built on it so the keyset cursor stays an index
-- range. SQLite's own lower() only folds ASCII, hence the explicit list.
-- cinetrack:statement
